WEBVTT

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:14.280
Congratulations on your graduation,

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:16.620
Utaha-senpai.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.840
Are you fine not going to the thank-you party?

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:59.970
I don't feel the slightest need to go there.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:02.520
When it comes to people in my class,

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:05.910
I feel absolutely no attachment whatsoever to them.

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:09.100
Those who wear a mask really do say things differently.

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:13.070
But I didn't think you'd come.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:16.740
We parted ways like that earlier, after all.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:21.410
<i>That may make Sawamura Eriri glad,</i>

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:25.750
<i>but I don't think Kashiwagi Eri is happy.</i>

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:31.670
That was a part of the reason I came today.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:33.920
We argued,

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:38.120
and I'm graduating, so it's probably the last time we meet,

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:39.680
so if we're parting ways anyway,

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:42.180
"I want to make memories, Utaha-senpai!",

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.130
you come to me,

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:45.050
aiming to do the dirty before dumping me for good?

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:45.850
No!

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:47.390
That's not where this is heading!

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:49.860
But if we're making memories,

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:53.150
could I just drop by my house and change into something nicer?

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:57.240
Oh, but if we're making graduation memories,
I guess the school uniform fetish is part of it too.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.510
I wonder which I should do!

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:03.450
Sorry, but I'd like to talk seriously here, so could you please shut up?

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:06.790
Utaha-senpai!

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.670
This is my answer.

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:15.460
Going forward, I really want to make a game together with the current members.

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:19.060
With you, Eriri, Michiru, me,

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:20.380
and with Katou.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.840
In order to do that,

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:25.720
I figured I could only create a plan in which everybody would want to participate.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:29.290
This proposal is for that?

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:30.480
Yes.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.980
Well then, I shall read it.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.730
Please do.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:00.470
Thank you.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:02.440
H-How was it?!

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:05.140
75 points.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.220
You did well, Morals-kun.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:11.540
The story and the setting aren't at all original,

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:14.380
but it goes for the clichés in a mostly well thought out manner.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:15.800
It isn't deliberately weird,

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:18.480
but works through the cuteness of the heroines.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:22.450
It indeed is a gal game-like approach, fitting for a moe game.

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:25.700
I don't mean that in a bad way, of course.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:29.590
I like romance stories and tear-jerkers like our previous game, too,

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:36.500
but I remembered that I first started the circle in order to convey the cuteness of the heroine to everybody.

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:39.970
Yes.

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:44.130
It says here very well what it is you want to make.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:46.300
You can tell those feelings from it.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:49.420
Thank you, Utaha-senpai.

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:52.310
I simply properly assessed this plan.

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:54.840
It's not something you need to be thankful for.

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:58.060
So,

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:00.940
would you participate in this plan?

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:06.410
If it's too much, even a little bit is fine.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.160
Just one route is enough.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:10.630
Even just supervising it is fine!

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:11.570
So...

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:13.660
Please!

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:22.310
Did you talk with Sawamura-san already?

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:23.680
Eriri?

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:25.420
What was her answer?

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.110
Did she say she'd join?

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:30.430
I haven't asked her yet.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:33.740
So I have to tell you, huh?

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:37.480
That's unfair, Sawamura-san.

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:41.190
Utaha-senpai?

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:44.440
I'm sorry, Tomoya-kun.

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:48.450
I can't continue with you.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:49.450
Huh?

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:54.700
Why?

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:59.680
I don't have any time to participate in your plan any more.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:01.930
I won't ask for anything unreasonable!

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:03.700
Not from you nor from Eriri!

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:05.390
Listen, Tomoya-kun.

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:11.720
You couldn't push anything unreasonable on Sawamura-san or on me.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:16.160
You couldn't even say that this is a plan worth throwing everything else aside for.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:21.430
There's... no way I could say something like that.

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:27.910
The moment you tell us creators that we don't have to do anything unreasonable, our progress grinds to a halt.

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:29.420
Having almost impossible deadlines,

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:32.180
fighting for a balance between quality and turning in the results early...

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:35.490
You can't improve if you don't struggle with those with your life on the line.

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:38.490
Utaha-senpai...

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:42.750
So Tomoya-kun, you're not fit to be a producer.

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:47.970
You have to become able to make people push their limits without doing anything.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:52.120
You have to show others hell while being able to pull back right away yourself.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:55.340
If you're unable to make the creators follow you so far that you feel bad about it,

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:56.880
you're a failure as a producer.

00:06:57.890 --> 00:07:02.560
Do such unreasonable people exist?

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:06.570
Someone told me to die for this plan.

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:11.770
But seeing the contents, I thought I wouldn't mind dying for it.

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:20.830
Wait a moment.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:22.950
Fields Chronicle...

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:24.840
Is it really <i>the</i> Fields Chronicle?

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:27.860
It's the 20th anniversary this year,

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:30.330
so apparently they're making a completely new one,

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:33.000
with new staff.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.100
You mean... Kousaka Akane?

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:38.120
It'll probably be a huge deal when it goes on sale.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:43.600
The hitmaker Kousaka Akane creating an epic RPG.

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:47.860
What is this?

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:53.410
If you were given your proposal and this one,

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:55.830
and asked which one you'd pick,

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:56.790
what would you do?

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:01.750
I'm sorry, Tomoya-kun.

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:06.520
In other words, Kousaka Akane scouted you?

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:07.920
By showing this?

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:11.080
Technically, it was a bit different.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:13.480
How exactly?

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:14.680
I'm sorry!

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:16.050
For what?!

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:19.890
The one Kousaka Akane is really after...

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:22.650
...is not me.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:32.900
Forgive me, Tomoya-kun!

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:39.290
<i>I became your number one!</i>

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:43.870
Of course you'd detest me.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:44.710
This can't be true.

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:50.290
But even so, I wanted to join forces with Kashiwagi Eri once more!

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:55.880
This can't be true!

00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:02.520
I'm sorry...

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:07.050
I'm sorry, Tomoya!

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:33.130
Let's see then...

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:38.390
Another failure?

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:44.570
It doesn't look that bad to me, though.

00:09:44.570 --> 00:09:46.250
What is it that you don't like about it?

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:49.220
How long have you been there, Kasumigaoka Utaha?!

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:50.400
Well,

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:55.320
from around the time you were grinning at Morals-kun's messages.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:59.420
"I will wait! I will always be waiting, Tomoya!", and such.

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:03.860
You have quite a gap between your tsun and dere.

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:06.170
It's almost like a split personality.

00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:09.040
Shut up, you stealthy long-black-hair!

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:12.390
Isn't that Katou-san these days?

00:10:12.390 --> 00:10:17.800
And anyway, whomever I wait for or go home with is none of your business!

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:20.040
Certainly, I don't mind,

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:23.520
but what if your friends see you together with him?

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:28.560
You've been hiding the circle and Morals-kun at all costs until now, haven't you?

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:30.320
We're just going home together.

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:32.150
I'm not guilty of anything.

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:33.880
Besides...

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:34.940
Besides?

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:41.660
Do you think I'd agree to still be friends with people who ask weird questions about it?

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:44.470
You're right.

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:47.160
Also, there's paint on your face.

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:53.170
Why aren't you going home?

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:56.380
You're not planning to come with us, are you?

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:59.630
I don't mean to be that childish.

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:03.400
Once we're done talking, I'll leave before he comes.

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:05.210
Talking about what?

00:11:05.210 --> 00:11:08.060
Do you still have other ways to tease me?

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:13.530
You were making the illustration for our circle's main page, weren't you?

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:15.370
When will it be done?

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:21.840
I believe the first deadline was in January.

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:23.710
We're already several days into February.

00:11:23.710 --> 00:11:25.440
I know!

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:28.200
I'm not telling you not to get so distracted over a guy.

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.800
I've been there myself.

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:32.140
It's not like I don't understand.

00:11:32.140 --> 00:11:34.210
I'm not losing myself over a guy.

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:36.650
And you haven't actually experienced it, have you?

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:39.080
But no matter whether it's doujin or commercial work,

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:41.400
finish your work properly.

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:43.110
You're a creator, aren't you?

00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:48.590
I just haven't completely recovered from my end-of-year flu.

00:11:48.590 --> 00:11:50.230
As soon as I'm back to normal...

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:53.780
Even though it's been over a month since the beginning of the year?

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:55.230
There's no helping it!

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:58.990
Somehow, I've become a crappy artist!

00:12:00.390 --> 00:12:04.990
I can't get anywhere close to the pictures I made in Nasu Highlands.

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:07.240
Aren't you just imagining it?

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:10.000
What do you know about drawing?

00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:17.500
Even so, earlier, you would have dealt with it somehow.

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:21.140
You'd have done the best you could within the time limit.

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:24.920
At the very least, you'd have stuck to it until the very end.

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:27.640
Where has your pride as a creator gone?

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:31.990
Where is the Sawamura Eriri who worked tirelessly at the end of the year in Nasu Highlands, until she collapsed-

00:12:31.990 --> 00:12:34.350
It's just an image for the page!

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:37.860
We're not selling it, and it doesn't affect the quality of the game!

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:39.400
Sawamura-san...

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:42.650
And now Tomoya forgives me for it.

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:48.370
Even if I don't draw anything, now him and I...

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:51.080
Perhaps so.

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:54.710
Well then, Sawamura-san.

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:01.630
Sorry I'm late.

00:13:02.680 --> 00:13:04.800
Did something happen?

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:06.800
No, it's nothing.

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:09.000
Let's go.

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:13.640
Maruzu?

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:14.680
Yes!

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:16.790
The game company from Osaka.

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:20.690
So even you, Shi-chan, who is not interested in anything but reading and younger guys,

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:22.780
do know about it!

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:26.910
Please don't say it like I'm a shotacon detached from earthly life.

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:32.620
Maruzu's games include a popular fantasy RPG series called Fields Chronicle.

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:36.080
And they asked <i>someone</i> to participate in the newest game.

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:37.160
Who did?

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:38.040
Maruzu did.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.140
Whom?

00:13:39.140 --> 00:13:40.920
Kasumi Utako-sensei.

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:45.210
We're actually already involved.

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:48.430
They have us publish the novelisation and the special magazines.

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:51.280
So I'd work on the novelisation of the game?

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:52.740
No.

00:13:52.740 --> 00:13:54.570
The main scenario for the game.

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:59.610
The higher-ups are rejoicing.

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:02.950
One of our authors would be the main writer for Fields Chronicle!

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:08.200
The winner of the copyright battle has basically been decided!

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:13.890
Do you even think I can do a fantasy RPG scenario?

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:15.790
Maybe a doujin, but other than that?

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:20.400
I think you can.

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:25.670
After all, Kasumi Utako's talent still has breadth and depth, with no end in sight.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:30.040
But I don't think it's time for that yet.

00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:33.530
I don't think you should be given to this person.

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:35.470
This person?

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:39.100
The one who made an offer to you by name.

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:41.930
A heavyweight even among pros,

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:46.510
who knows everything about both doujin and
commercial publishing, even the dark side of it.

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:47.990
Who is it?

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:51.740
Kousaka Akane.

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:54.470
From Rouge en Rouge?

00:14:54.470 --> 00:14:58.280
Though it appears she has her younger associates take care of the doujin circle.

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:01.090
But in commercial publishing, for some years now,

00:15:01.090 --> 00:15:06.960
she's been a popular original mangaka
whose works sell over a million copies.

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:11.930
Why does such a superior creator approach someone like me?

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:14.470
Apparently she found what she was looking for by playing this.

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:19.940
A scenario writer and an illustrator fitting for her next project.

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:22.400
Illustrator,

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:23.560
too?

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:27.440
Are you okay with this, Sawamura-san?

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:30.700
Just coming here even though you're not planning on taking the job?

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:32.410
It can't be helped.

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:35.770
You said you'd have to at least show up.

00:15:35.770 --> 00:15:40.260
I have to come because I have my
obligations for Fushikawa Bookstore.

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:41.120
But you-

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:42.290
If you were alone,

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:45.370
they'd talk you into doing it before you know it.

00:15:45.370 --> 00:15:48.470
That's not really something you need to worry about...

00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:53.680
I don't care in the least if you were to disappear, but it'll be trouble for Tomoya.

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:55.250
Sawamura-san...

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:59.110
He's not saying much about it,

00:15:59.110 --> 00:16:01.930
but it appears he's thinking about the next game.

00:16:01.930 --> 00:16:06.940
There's no way he can recover from losing his main writer at that point!

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:13.910
Your guests have arrived.

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:19.410
Excuse me.

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:24.730
H-Hey,

00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:26.920
you're from Maruzu, right?

00:16:27.490 --> 00:16:28.960
Hm?

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:33.940
Kousaka Akane!

00:16:33.940 --> 00:16:34.740
What?

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:36.300
Kousaka Akane?!

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:37.240
Her?

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:38.260
No way...

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:40.270
Ah...

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:43.590
It's been a while, Kashiwagi-sensei.

00:16:43.590 --> 00:16:46.020
So, how have you been since then?

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:48.520
Have we met somewhere?

00:16:49.990 --> 00:16:51.530
I wonder.

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:52.960
It's just you?

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:54.690
What about the representative from Maruzu?

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:57.500
We need no big shots from the company.

00:16:57.500 --> 00:17:01.270
Only creators are allowed here today.

00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:03.540
You have thirty minutes to read it.

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:05.580
Then decide.

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:07.410
Decide what?

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:10.840
Whether you will get on board that plan or not.

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:12.880
What nonsense are you spouting?

00:17:13.160 --> 00:17:16.050
The series has been going for twenty years.

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:19.680
I wouldn't like to think my story is that half-baked.

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:21.350
That's not what I'm saying!

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:24.870
I'm telling you not to get ahead of yourself!

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:27.740
We haven't said a word about participating-

00:17:27.740 --> 00:17:28.730
Hey!

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:30.610
What are you opening it for, Kasumigaoka Utaha?

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:33.040
Won't you look, Sawamura-san?

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:35.860
Hey, wait, you!

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:39.370
It's Kousaka Akane's proposal.

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:42.200
Her work.

00:18:04.670 --> 00:18:07.650
Opinions, questions, criticisms, anything, bring it on.

00:18:07.650 --> 00:18:11.060
Only if you're confident enough to pick a fight over it, though.

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:16.960
What is it that you want us to do?

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:20.320
Die.

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:25.080
You are to give your lives for this game.

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:26.310
For an entire year,

00:18:26.310 --> 00:18:28.410
you keep thinking about this game,

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:30.140
you live for this game,

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:32.580
you devote your entire lives for this game.

00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:34.500
What's that all of a sudden?!

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:36.270
Kashiwagi Eri.

00:18:36.270 --> 00:18:41.090
The last seven pictures of the game you released earlier.

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:42.550
That's it.

00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:44.490
That's what I want.

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:45.310
No,

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:47.560
go way above that!

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:50.060
If you don't, there's no point in having you.

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:51.860
What are you spouting?!

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:53.900
There's no way I can agree to that!

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:57.770
I have a circle... Blessing Software!

00:18:57.770 --> 00:19:01.570
But you can't stay in that circle any more, can you?

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:07.700
If things stay like they are, people around you will be overwhelmed by your talent.

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:10.830
Nobody will be able to keep up with you.

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:12.430
That's not true!

00:19:12.430 --> 00:19:14.490
It is!

00:19:14.490 --> 00:19:19.050
Kasumi Utako is the only one there who can just about keep up.

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:25.180
So Kasumi Utako, your role will be to draw out Kashiwagi Eri's skills.

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:28.090
Both technically and mentally.

00:19:28.090 --> 00:19:31.840
I would be Sawamura-san's assistant?

00:19:31.840 --> 00:19:35.650
I do think highly of the scenario you did for that game.

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:39.360
But if Kashiwagi Eri is not joining,

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:42.120
there's no point in insisting Kasumi Utako join.

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:45.830
I-I can't do such a huge job.

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:48.410
It's an amazing opportunity,

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:50.830
but I can't draw like back then any more.

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:53.190
What, a bit of a slump?

00:19:53.190 --> 00:19:54.560
Not just a bit!

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:56.870
I'm at my limit! I can't draw like that ever again!

00:19:56.870 --> 00:19:57.960
Sawamura-san!

00:20:14.170 --> 00:20:16.730
Are you kidding me, you scribbler?!

00:20:22.110 --> 00:20:24.720
You're nowhere close to peaking yet!

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:27.780
You transformed just once, and you're already saying you're in a slump?!

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:29.490
Stop insulting artists!

00:20:29.960 --> 00:20:31.200
Stop...

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:33.540
You're not in a slump or anything!

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:35.040
You're just shitty!

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:36.420
Your skills just aren't there yet!

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:37.420
Stop...

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:39.500
That's enough!

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:45.650
Because you know,

00:20:45.650 --> 00:20:49.760
your pictures are like this, right?

00:21:01.610 --> 00:21:05.240
Those are original, so I do respect you.

00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:08.240
No way...

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:12.000
But it can still be easily copied...

00:21:12.820 --> 00:21:14.430
Your style.
